# Runtime / generated artifacts
alerts.db
# SQLite WAL sidecars. These were tracked, which is why they appeared to be
# "deleted" whenever the database was closed cleanly: SQLite checkpoints the WAL
# into the main file and removes them. A WAL is a transient journal, never
# source, and committing one only produces confusing diffs.
alerts.db-wal
alerts.db-shm
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
alerts/
clips/
videos/
snapshots/
DEMO_OUTPUTS/
*.log